# The CPython release both desktop installers bundle (issue #261).
#
# One file because there are two builds. The .dmg and the .exe each carry their own
# interpreter, from the same python-build-standalone release, in a different triple:
#
#   macOS    aarch64-apple-darwin / x86_64-apple-darwin
#   Windows  x86_64-pc-windows-msvc               (x64 only; ARM runs it emulated)
#
# Typed twice, the two could be edited apart, and nothing would look wrong: each build
# would succeed, each installer would launch, and one version number would name two
# different applications. So `build/mac/build_dmg.sh` sources this file and
# `build/windows/build_installer.bat` reads it with `for /f "tokens=1,2 delims=="`.
#
# That pair of readers is why the grammar here is `KEY=value` and nothing else: no quotes,
# no spaces around the `=`, no continuations, nothing `cmd.exe` cannot parse.
# `tests/test_windows_installer.py` holds the file inside that intersection, since the one
# place a broken line would surface is a build machine where nobody runs the suite.
#
# To move the pin, change these two values and delete `.python_cache` in both build
# directories. Both are downloaded from
# https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases
#
# Before lowering it, read `requirements.txt`: this interpreter is the one that has to
# install the app's dependencies on first launch, so their floors are its floor. It cannot
# go below what pip will resolve for them, and a version that fails to resolve is not a
# broken build - it is an installer that completes and then cannot start, which is the exact
# failure issue #261 exists to remove.
PYTHON_VERSION=3.11.15
PYTHON_TAG=20260303
